    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {"@context":"http://schema.org","@graph":[{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-12T08:00:14.369Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":172},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_opinion-on-the-provision-of-non-mica-compliant-activity-7515320413040734208-rgx5","text":"❌ #MiCA-authorised #crypto-asset service providers should no longer provide services related to stablecoins that do not comply with the regulation to EU clients → https://lnkd.in/eTKUVnke \n\n📋 ESMA’s opinion sets supervisory expectations for services involving asset-referenced tokens (ARTs) and e-money tokens (EMTs), commonly known as stablecoins, that do not comply with MiCA requirements.\n\n🪙 The expectations cover the full range of crypto-asset services under MiCA, from trading and exchange services to custody, transfers, investment advice and portfolio management.\n\nMore in the opinion 👇","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_opinion-on-the-provision-of-non-mica-compliant-activity-7515320413040734208-rgx5"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-11T07:04:32.200Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":83},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_esma-activity-7514944007102353408-gwbi","text":"🔵 ESMA has appointed Carlos San Basilio (CNMV), as the new member of its Management Board → https://lnkd.in/dSwz2q7Y.\n\nHe replaces carlo comporti (CONSOB), who will take up the role of #ESMA Chair on 1 November → https://lnkd.in/dapveWRT.\n\n💡 DYK | The Management Board ensures that ESMA carries out its mission and the responsibilities set out in its founding Regulation → https://lnkd.in/dZHMzNDg.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_esma-activity-7514944007102353408-gwbi"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-09T08:36:23.945Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":420},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_carlo-comporti-appointed-chair-of-esma-activity-7514242349309374464-XyDQ","text":"🥁 Meet #ESMA’s next Chair: carlo comporti will take up the role on 1 November 2026 → https://lnkd.in/dapveWRT\n\nWith decades of experience in financial regulation and a strong understanding of ESMA, Carlo steps into the role at a pivotal time for the European financial markets.\n\n👏 A heartfelt thank you to Verena Ross for her outstanding leadership over the past five years and for helping shape ESMA into the organisation it is today.\n\nWe look forward to welcoming Carlo to the #ESMAteam!","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_carlo-comporti-appointed-chair-of-esma-activity-7514242349309374464-XyDQ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-08T08:00:21.092Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":33},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_extended-transitional-period-for-third-country-activity-7513870889776640001-9pPZ","text":"EU market participants should not be prevented from accessing the services of third-country central securities depositories (CSDs) beyond 17 January 2027 and until the EU finalises the relevant legislation. 📄 Read our statement → https://lnkd.in/e69AhhRg\n\n💡 The clarification addresses uncertainty ahead of the proposed extension of the current transitional regime and supports the orderly functioning of EU #CapitalMarkets.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_extended-transitional-period-for-third-country-activity-7513870889776640001-9pPZ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-07T08:01:04.432Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":79},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_eucareers-esmateam-activity-7513508683696496640-flDJ","text":"🎓 ESMA joined the #EUCareers Fair organised by the Swedish Council for Higher Education (UHR) in Stockholm, where more than 2,500 participants explored opportunities in the EU institutions.\n\n⭐ Connecting with talented students and professionals allowed us to share a behind-the-scenes look at what it is like to work at ESMA. Thank you to everyone who stopped by!\n\n📸 Check out a few highlights from the day 👇\n📌 Learn more about #ESMAteam → https://lnkd.in/dhBvxPNW ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_eucareers-esmateam-activity-7513508683696496640-flDJ"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-06T08:01:31.303Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":58},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_working-paper-on-haircuts-and-borrower-concentration-activity-7513146408535982080-ocSv","text":"What role do relationships and bargaining power play in determining risk? According to #ESMA’s latest working paper, more than you might expect. \n🔎 The research finds that borrowing conditions in EU repo markets are not determined solely by the quality of collateral exchanged. They are also influenced by factors such as a borrower’s bargaining power, competition between lenders, the diversification of its funding sources, and the strength of relationships between counterparties.\n\n🔑 Why does this matter? As attention increasingly turns to vulnerabilities outside the banking sector, understanding how these factors influence borrowing conditions can provide valuable insights into leverage, market resilience, and financial stability.\n\n📘 Read the full paper to learn more about the factors shaping borrowing conditions and bilateral haircuts in EU repo markets and their implications for #financial stability → https://lnkd.in/dQuERsYx","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_working-paper-on-haircuts-and-borrower-concentration-activity-7513146408535982080-ocSv"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-05T08:00:17.693Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":167},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_green-finance-dashboard-2q2026-activity-7512783711923515394-mW97","text":"🟢 Our new green finance dashboard for Q2 2026 is now live → https://lnkd.in/dNdF6wxY\nKey findings show resilient #ESG markets, though with mixed developments across segments, alongside growing ESG private fund assets and EU ESG bonds.\n\nTake a look at the latest trends shaping #SustainableFinance. 👇📊 The dashboard will be updated quarterly, providing a regular snapshot of developments across sustainable finance markets.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_green-finance-dashboard-2q2026-activity-7512783711923515394-mW97"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-02T08:00:07.680Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":61},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_esmas-proposals-on-mica-review-activity-7511696506329026561-7p9V","text":"🛡️ The review of #MiCA offers an opportunity to strengthen the EU framework for #crypto-assets. In our response to the European Commission's consultation, we set out recommendations to ensure the rules remain clear, safe, and capable of addressing emerging developments → https://lnkd.in/d3AS77QE\n\n🎯 The proposals aim to support investor protection, regulatory consistency, and innovation across the EU.\n👇 Swipe through the slides to see our key recommendations.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_esmas-proposals-on-mica-review-activity-7511696506329026561-7p9V"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-10-01T08:08:32.072Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":31},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_data-day-2026-agenda-activity-7511336234041139200-DSvH","text":"How can data support more effective supervision? What role will artificial intelligence, RegTech and SupTech play in the future of financial markets? And how can Europe make better use of regulatory data for investors and market participants?\n\n⚡ Join us in Paris on 24 November 2026 for #DataDay to discuss the future of financial data and reporting. 🪑 𝐀𝐭𝐭𝐞𝐧𝐝 𝐢𝐧 𝐩𝐞𝐫𝐬𝐨𝐧 𝐭𝐨 𝐠𝐞𝐭 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐟𝐮𝐥𝐥 𝐞𝐱𝐩𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐞𝐧𝐜𝐞! Several sessions will take place in breakout rooms and will not be streamed or recorded, making on-site participation the only way to access all discussions and exchanges. Find more details about registration → https://lnkd.in/e_sCkgNm \n\n💬 The agenda (https://lnkd.in/dC_u6FJQ) includes: \n- Keynote speech by Markus Ferber, MdEP, Member of the European Parliament\n-  Fireside chat with Nicolas Vasse (executive director, AMLA - The EU Anti-Money Laundering Authority) and Natasha Cazenave (executive director, #ESMA)\n- Discussions on AI, RegTech and SupTech, fund reporting, crypto monitoring under MiCA, transaction reporting, and ESAP\nDedicated break-out sessions and opportunities to engage directly with experts and peers ","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_data-day-2026-agenda-activity-7511336234041139200-DSvH"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"SocialMediaPosting","author":{"@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma"},"datePublished":"2026-09-30T08:01:14.742Z","interactionStatistic":{"@type":"InteractionCounter","interactionType":"http://schema.org/LikeAction","userInteractionCount":35},"mainEntityOfPage":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_working-paper-on-margining-repo-transactions-activity-7510972011880452096-ya1N","text":"In an environment marked by market volatility and shifting sovereign bond yields, how resilient are the safeguards that underpin short-term funding #markets? 🔎 Our new working paper examines margin practices in European repo markets, drawing on #SFTR data and evidence from recent episodes of stress in government bond markets → https://lnkd.in/dxRcgJTW \n\n💡 The findings provide new insights into how these risk buffers are used across different market segments and how they evolve during periods of market stress. Understanding these dynamics is key to assessing market resilience and financial stability.","url":"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma_working-paper-on-margining-repo-transactions-activity-7510972011880452096-ya1N"},{"@context":"http://schema.org","@type":"Organization","name":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","url":"https://fr.linkedin.com/company/european-securities-and-markets-authority-esma","address":{"type":"PostalAddress","streetAddress":"201-203, Rue de Bercy","addressLocality":"Paris","addressRegion":"Île-de-France","postalCode":"75012","addressCountry":"FR"},"description":"ESMA is an independent EU Authority that was established in 2011.  It works closely with the national competent authorities who are members of the European System of Financial Supervision and the other European Supervisory Authorities – the European Banking Authority (EBA) responsible for banking and the European Insurance and Occupational Pensions Authority (EIOPA) responsible for insurance and occupational pensions.\n\nContact information: https://www.esma.europa.eu/contact-information","numberOfEmployees":{"value":566,"@type":"QuantitativeValue"},"logo":{"contentUrl":"https://media.licdn.com/dms/image/v2/D4D0BAQGf01LHlAgrrQ/company-logo_200_200/B4DZ8ogDHqGwAI-/0/1783090918077/european_securities_and_markets_authority_esma_logo?e=2147483647&v=beta&t=DaX-zqBeH7AUt6F5gjN88Gl1Yvc9cSpUWufJ_oNQh2Y","description":"European Securities and Markets Authority (ESMA)","@type":"ImageObject"},"slogan":"EU authority responsible for enhancing investor protection, promoting orderly markets & ensuring financial stability.","sameAs":"http://www.esma.europa.eu"}]}
    </script>
  
  
      
