    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">❌ <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fmica&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#MiCA</a>-authorised <a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Fcrypto&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#crypto</a>-asset service providers should no longer provide services related to stablecoins that do not comply with the regulation to EU clients → <a class="link" href="https://lnkd.in/eTKUVnke?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" rel="nofollow" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>https://lnkd.in/eTKUVnke</a> 

📋 ESMA’s opinion sets supervisory expectations for services involving asset-referenced tokens (ARTs) and e-money tokens (EMTs), commonly known as stablecoins, that do not comply with MiCA requirements.

🪙 The expectations cover the full range of crypto-asset services under MiCA, from trading and exchange services to custody, transfers, investment advice and portfolio management.

More in the opinion 👇</p>
